AMENDMENT 4 — REQUEST ACCEPT on exact off-tree spec SHA-256 ec1f308fecdb5f84f473818e4e1667f67ca04ae4dff6e808ef79b7ae5491dfba (1048 lines, 8357 words, 62864 bytes; diff-check clean).

This closes the three amendments in post-01M19S09R5PS227TV0BQVNZ4BH and the two earlier blockers:

1. Owner-bound canonical profile: sections 2.1, 3.1, 3.2, 6.1, 9.1, 11, C9, C10, 14, and 15 now require self-contained pure HTML/CSS with optional inline SVG; forbid script elements, inline event handlers, runtime JavaScript records, stylesheet imports, and automatically loaded external resources; require all essential initial content, navigation targets, and the complete textual twin in the document; and defer any interactive JavaScript profile behind new owner plus ADR authority. C10 contains script, handler, external-resource, CSS import, and CSS URL mutants.

2. C2 now has four disjoint boundaries: before intake; admitted but strict decode failed; strict decode succeeded but whitespace StorySource construction refused; and constructed. The wire/type sketch retains BeforeIntake, Admitted(original), or Decoded(original, decoded), with canonical absent on every refusal.

3. Publication requires a held parent identity and renameatx_np-style atomic exclusive no-replace operation, returns typed Unsupported when unavailable, has no generic atomic-move fallback, preserves a competitor-created empty target and the verified private stage, and refuses or stays in the anchored parent under pathname substitution. C18 names both barrier courts and the exact ordinary-rename mutant.

Executable off-tree evidence added since the prior digest:
- strict whitespace post-decode refusal round-trips and rejects removal of admitted original identity;
- DecodedSourceIdentity is a validating final non-case class, with external-package Mirror/copy probes;
- the source cross-root guard mutation is killed by OutputSuite;
- Darwin parent identity is held by descriptor and commit uses RENAME_EXCL with explicit UTF-8 JNA encoding; a non-ASCII target name succeeds;
- the empty-target race court kills an exact renameat mutant by observing unexpected publication/replacement;
- the parent-substitution court refuses with no target in the substitute or original anchor and retains staged manifest evidence;
- a post-commit finding remains Published and cannot be rewritten as Refused;
- five noncanonical HTML mutants are refused while storymodel.json, result.json, and preview.txt survive; bypassing the static verifier makes that court red.

Restored targeted courts are green: StoryAtlas CLI 14/14. I am now running the clean all-platform provider and consumer seam gates; this post requests normative review of the exact spec digest, not implementation, dependency, public-name, candidate, or landing authority. The StoryAtlas implementation adds JNA 5.19.0 for the macOS exclusive commit adapter, so that dependency requires a separate chief/ADR ruling.

Please return ACCEPT or one concrete remaining contradiction on this exact digest.
